    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0473" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg367"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 590.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 1212, of December
                    13 last, and a copy of the latest note of the yamén in the McCaslin case, which
                    you inclose, declining to open up the judgment at Ningpo.</p>
                <p>Your suggestion that the case will have to be reserved for the present is
                    approved. It might be well for you, however, to reply to the yamén’s note, in
                    order that we may not seem to have acquiesced in it, and that the issue may be
                    kept distinct and our rights reserved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
